I'm marketing fundamentals faculty chair  and simply learn presenting programmatic  foundations in this course we're going  to cover the basics of programmatic  advertising what it is and how you can  make it work for you  programmatic at its core is automating  the buying and selling of advertising  media using technology if you've gone to  Google AdWords and you've set up an  account and you've developed ads to be  shown for a specific search phrase then  you've developed a programmatic ad you  have creative and you have established  that it will only be shown upon a  specific trigger such as the search  phrase you've automated the display and  the trigger of that creative to be shown  to a user who shows themself to be  relevant in looking for what you have  that's the basis of programmatic is  automating the system of buying and  selling ads using technology now you can  use this system for branding to increase  your reach and awareness for a campaign  specific objective also we are most  familiar with retargeting that is  putting an ad in front of a user that  has been to your website we can also use  programmatic marketing and ads for lead  generation we can target them to display  on a specific device to go in a specific  channel and we can also use those  campaigns to develop existing customers  by presenting customer specific  campaigns based on their history their  purchase history or specific campaigns  based on a characteristic programmatic  encompasses a wide variety of media  usually when people think of  programmatic they think of display ads  the banner ads are the rectangle ads  that show on a website when you go to an  any news site or content site display  ads are part of programmatic you can  create a creative to show in those spots  and bid in order to put them there  that's one of the primary ways that  people use programmatic but you can also  develop rich media to display in any one  of those areas and define at which point  a rich media ad will show instead of a  static creative you can also define the  channel so that your ad displays in a  user's social feed and you can target  specific people based on characteristics  and have your ad be presented to them  just specifically in their social theme  you can create a custom audience through  Facebook where you take your own  audience you upload it into Facebook and  you can target your users utilizing  Facebook and present a custom message to  your users you can also develop this and  bid on video to be shown to specific  users that can be shown as a pre-roll  video ad when they go to youtube or  another video site or you can even bid  on that video to be shown to a user  within the context of a website that  they would go to in this example we see  a video ad from Microsoft playing on  forbes.com because it was a specific  user that was targeted to receive that  information and the advertiser Microsoft  has also bid on the ability to put a  video rather than just a static display  ad part of programmatic is also focusing  on the device that I can show ads  specifically on a mobile device or  specifically a laptop or desktop based  on what I want the user to do ads on  mobile right now are performing at a  higher and  rate then ads on desktops or laptops in  fact mobile ads have an 18 percent on  average click-through rate which is  higher than desktops or laptops what is  really doing well in mobile is mobile  video consumers are watching a massive  amount of video on their mobile devices  and so ad revenue in the mobile video  arena is estimated to go three times as  much as desktop advertising be aware  because of the higher competition it's  going to cost more to bid on mobile ads  specifically targeted to users where  they will be in the content they are  viewing included in mobile is the  ability to buy ad space on apps app  developers as a different way or an  additional way to monetize their apps  can open up inventory for advertisers to  bid on ad space within the app that way  you can bid to reach people through an  app on their device through their social  stream and you can determine which type  of ad they can see in any one of these  channels marketing Sherpa did a study on  advertisers and saw that their average  conversion rates were somewhere between  one and a half to four percent based on  the channel where they receive the lead  so search has an average conversion rate  of about almost four percent paid search  almost three percent webinars generated  leads but only had a conversion rate of  about up 1.6 percent social media almost  2 percent and a lead to opportunity  conversion rate however advertisers that  didn't just rely on the initial  conversion but followed up with  programmatic ad targeting techniques saw  an improvement of over 32 percent and  their cost per acquisition returns so  utilizing programmatic as an additional  layer  of using these advanced abilities to  target users based on their behavior  demographic characteristics or your own  customers based on purchase history or  history with the company you can enhance  each campaign and you can improve your  campaigns are using these targeting  techniques to meet people in real time  and what we've seen is that when ads are  delivered to people in real time based  on behavior that they just exhibited or  a site that they recently visited they  are twice as likely to interact with it  than an ad that is not based on their  behavior advertisers can bid to get  their ads in front of people in the most  critical time period of all and that's  real time immediately after a certain  behavior or a site visit they can  interact with those customers and get  the right ad the right ad media and the  right network to be in front of the  right user at the right time this is  programmatic foundations  I'm Matt Bailey thank you for watching  the introduction and I look forward to  seeing you and further modules  you
 

